msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "Lua (mods' scripts): MIT"
msgstr "Lua (les scripts des mods) : MIT"

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "DXVK: zlib (Linux packages)"
msgstr "DXVK : zlib (paquets Linux)"

#. %1 is a licence file's path, %2 HIRAKU's folder
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "%1 was not found in the HIRAKU folder (%2)."
msgstr "%1 est introuvable dans le dossier de HIRAKU (%2)."

#. one credit in About > Software: %1 the software's name, %2 its licence and holders, %3 what it does in HIRAKU
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "<b>%1</b> (%2): %3"
msgstr "<b>%1</b> (%2) : %3"

#. one reference in About > Software: %1 its name, %2 what it was used for
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "<b>%1</b>: %2"
msgstr "<b>%1</b> : %2"

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "Konami arcade games as native programs, on Linux and Windows. Firebeat games run their PowerPC code recompiled (or, in a package, through HIRAKU's own analysis of it); DJ Main, System 573, Twinkle and Python run on the same shell, behind this launcher."
msgstr "Les jeux d'arcade Konami en programmes natifs, sous Linux et Windows. Les jeux Firebeat exécutent leur code PowerPC recompilé (ou, dans un paquet, au travers de l'analyse qu'en fait HIRAKU) ; DJ Main, System 573, Twinkle et Python tournent sur le même socle, derrière ce lanceur."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "HIRAKU ships no game data. It runs your own dumps."
msgstr "HIRAKU ne fournit aucune donnée de jeu. Il fait tourner vos propres dumps."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "The licence notice below is legal text, kept in English."
msgstr "La notice de licence ci-dessous est un texte juridique : elle reste en anglais."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "Code taken from other projects keeps its own licence and notices: see Software and Licences."
msgstr "Le code repris d'autres projets garde sa propre licence et ses mentions : voir Logiciels et Licences."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "%1 are trademarks of Konami. HIRAKU is not affiliated with or endorsed by Konami."
msgstr "%1 sont des marques de Konami. HIRAKU n'est ni affilié à Konami ni approuvé par Konami."

#. %1 the Qt version HIRAKU was built with, %2 the one it runs on
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "Built with Qt %1, running on Qt %2."
msgstr "Compilé avec Qt %1, exécuté avec Qt %2."

#. who holds a code's copyright, in About > Software: %1 a project's or person's name
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "%1 and contributors"
msgstr "%1 et ses contributeurs"

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the sp2xdev team and the SpiceTools contributors"
msgstr "l'équipe sp2xdev et les contributeurs de SpiceTools"

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "Code in HIRAKU"
msgstr "Code présent dans HIRAKU"

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the devices of the XT446 synth card, System 573, Twinkle and the multi-session unit, on HIRAKU's own shim of MAME's framework. Copyright holders are named in each file."
msgstr "les composants de la carte synthé XT446, du System 573, de Twinkle et de l'unité multi-session, sur la couche d'adaptation de HIRAKU au framework de MAME. Les titulaires des droits sont nommés dans chaque fichier."

#. %1 a person's online name
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "%1's System 573 work"
msgstr "le travail de %1 sur le System 573"

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the multi-session unit, its TC9446F MP3 decoders, SIO1 as a UART, the TX3927 CPU."
msgstr "l'unité multi-session, ses décodeurs MP3 TC9446F, SIO1 comme UART, le processeur TX3927."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the 68000 of the Firebeat SPU and the 68EC020 of DJ Main."
msgstr "le 68000 du SPU Firebeat et le 68EC020 du DJ Main."

#. %1 the licence and holders of SoftFloat 3 (names: keep them)
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "release 2b in Musashi; Berkeley SoftFloat 3 (%1) in the MIPS CPUs."
msgstr "la version 2b dans Musashi ; Berkeley SoftFloat 3 (%1) dans les processeurs MIPS."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the MP3 decoding of the 573's digital I/O board and the multi-session unit."
msgstr "le décodage MP3 de la carte d'E/S numérique du 573 et de l'unité multi-session."

#. %1 libchdr (a link), %2 its licence and holders, %3 dr_flac, %4 its holder, %5 the LZMA SDK, %6 its holder
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "<b>%1</b> (%2), with %3 (public domain or MIT-0, %4) and the %5's decoder (public domain, %6): MAME's CHDs read in place."
msgstr "<b>%1</b> (%2), avec %3 (domaine public ou MIT-0, %4) et le décodeur du %5 (domaine public, %6) : les CHD de MAME lus tels quels."

#. %1 and %2 the shaders' authors' names (keep them)
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "crt-guest-advanced-fast (%1) and crt-royale (%2), the picture's CRT shaders."
msgstr "crt-guest-advanced-fast (%1) et crt-royale (%2), les shaders CRT de l'image."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the analog CRT picture, the signal, the TV and the tube."
msgstr "l'image CRT analogique : le signal, le téléviseur et le tube."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "a CRT's rolling scan on a fast display."
msgstr "le balayage progressif d'un CRT sur un écran rapide."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the language of mods' scripts."
msgstr "le langage des scripts des mods."

#. %1 and %2 are the makers of two protocols (names: keep them)
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "presentation-time (%1) and fifo-v1 (%2), for frame pacing."
msgstr "presentation-time (%1) et fifo-v1 (%2), pour la cadence des images."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the 64-bit PC loader's start-up of AVS2 games, its two-screen Direct3D 9, its board, card reader and licence-key stand-ins and its touch screen, written after spice2x's."
msgstr "le démarrage des jeux AVS2 par le chargeur PC 64 bits, son Direct3D 9 à deux écrans, ses substituts de carte, de lecteur de carte et de clé de licence et son écran tactile, écrits d'après ceux de spice2x."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the binary XML of pop'n music 17 and 18's e-AMUSEMENT, written from its description of the format."
msgstr "le XML binaire de l'e-AMUSEMENT de pop'n music 17 et 18, écrit d'après sa description du format."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "Libraries"
msgstr "Bibliothèques"

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "this launcher."
msgstr "ce lanceur."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "windows, sound, controllers and their LEDs."
msgstr "fenêtres, son, manettes et leurs LED."

#. %1 PCSX2 Reliquary (a link), %2 PCSX2 (a link)
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "<b>%1</b> (GPL-3.0-or-later), a fork of %2: the emulator inside the Konami Python core."
msgstr "<b>%1</b> (GPL-3.0-or-later), un fork de %2 : l'émulateur au cœur de Konami Python."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "LGPL-2.1-or-later; GPL-2.0-or-later as built with x264"
msgstr "LGPL-2.1-or-later ; GPL-2.0-or-later tel que compilé avec x264"

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "Twinkle's background video and the games' video recordings, when found at build time."
msgstr "la vidéo de fond de Twinkle et les enregistrements vidéo des jeux, s'il est trouvé à la compilation."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "H.264 recordings on the processor, inside the packages' FFmpeg."
msgstr "les enregistrements H.264 par le processeur, dans le FFmpeg des paquets."

#. %1 nv-codec-headers (a link), %2 AMD AMF (a link)
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "<b>%1</b> and <b>%2</b> headers (MIT): H.264 recordings on NVIDIA and AMD graphics cards, with their drivers."
msgstr "en-têtes <b>%1</b> et <b>%2</b> (MIT) : les enregistrements H.264 sur les cartes graphiques NVIDIA et AMD, avec leurs pilotes."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "Apache-2.0 or MIT"
msgstr "Apache-2.0 ou MIT"

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "H.264 recordings by Vulkan video (AMD and Intel cards), with their drivers."
msgstr "les enregistrements H.264 par Vulkan Video (cartes AMD et Intel), avec leurs pilotes."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "Keyboardmania's SoundFont stand-in for the XT446, when found at build time."
msgstr "le substitut SoundFont de la XT446 pour Keyboardmania, s'il est trouvé à la compilation."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the launcher's icons."
msgstr "les icônes du lanceur."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "Direct3D 9 on Vulkan for the 64-bit PC games under Wine, in the Linux packages."
msgstr "Direct3D 9 sur Vulkan pour les jeux PC 64 bits sous Wine, dans les paquets Linux."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "References"
msgstr "Références"

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the oracle every core is checked against, frame by frame and access by access."
msgstr "la référence à laquelle chaque cœur est comparé, image par image et accès par accès."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the oracle for the Python core."
msgstr "la référence du cœur Python."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the analysis of each game program before translation."
msgstr "l'analyse de chaque programme de jeu avant sa traduction."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the reference for the PowerPC instruction tests."
msgstr "la référence des tests d'instructions PowerPC."

#. %1 and %2 are people's online names (keep them); reader/ and games/iidx/ are folders
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the names and meanings of the e-AMUSEMENT options, and the real card readers' and the BIO2 board's dialogue (its reader/ and games/iidx/); its cardio (%1) and PC/SC (%2) readers (MIT) for what those readers send; for the PC pop'n games, the I/O board's and the card reader's DLL interfaces (ezusb, libacio) and the e-AMUSEMENT services they ask for."
msgstr "les noms et le sens des options e-AMUSEMENT, et le dialogue des vrais lecteurs de carte et de la carte BIO2 (ses dossiers reader/ et games/iidx/) ; ses lecteurs cardio (%1) et PC/SC (%2) (MIT) pour ce que ces lecteurs envoient ; pour les jeux pop'n PC, les interfaces DLL de la carte d'E/S et du lecteur de carte (ezusb, libacio) et les services e-AMUSEMENT qu'ils demandent."

#. %1 a person's online name (keep it)
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "the ideas behind presses judged when they happened, the board's samples for pop'n music 16-18, the PIN typed for the player and mods that replace text (popnhax has no licence: none of its code is in HIRAKU); and %1's PopnForwarder and advice on the pop'n board."
msgstr "les idées derrière les appuis jugés au moment où ils ont lieu, les sons de la carte pour pop'n music 16-18, le code PIN saisi pour le joueur et les mods qui remplacent du texte (popnhax n'a pas de licence : rien de son code n'est dans HIRAKU) ; et le PopnForwarder de %1 et ses conseils sur la carte pop'n."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "its ezusb2-popn emulation, a check of the pop'n board's packets."
msgstr "son émulation ezusb2-popn, une vérification des paquets de la carte pop'n."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "a reference for e-AMUSEMENT servers and the later games' settings."
msgstr "une référence pour les serveurs e-AMUSEMENT et les réglages des jeux récents."

#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "event codes, unlocks and song facts."
msgstr "codes d'événement, déblocages et informations sur les chansons."

#. %1 the testers' names, as a list ("a, b and c")
#: launcher/aboutdialog.cpp
#, qt-format
msgctxt "AboutDialog"
msgid "Thanks to the testers, %1, who tried HIRAKU on their own PCs and cabinets, and to everyone who dumped, documented and preserved these machines."
msgstr "Merci aux testeurs, %1, qui ont essayé HIRAKU sur leurs PC et leurs bornes, et à tous ceux qui ont dumpé, documenté et préservé ces machines."

